      "message": "$index belongs in this list alongside the bus index. It is widely used for the same purpose — upstream\u0027s own NVMe and PSU configurations name instances \"NVMe $index\" with an identity-only probe — and it has the same defect the paragraph describes, for the same reason: it is assigned by iterating the discovered-object map, so it reflects discovery order rather than topology, and it renumbers the remaining devices when one is absent. If the design displaces bus-derived location identity, it would be worth saying whether $index is displaced too.",
